# L §4.2, §7.6 item 5 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): a calendar whose weekends name all seven days has no business
# day: add_business and schedule, which seek one, refuse it (RUN-DOMAIN calendar cal has no business day); is_business
# answers false; a calendar of six weekend days finds Sunday 2026-03-08. tally 2.1.5's refcore walked add_business to
# 9999-12-31 (REFCORE-NOT-YET).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input cal: calendar
input cal6: calendar
input d0: date
input dom: int

def nb: date = add_business(d0, 1, cal) at reader
def nb6: date = add_business(d0, 1, cal6) at reader
def ib: bool = is_business(d0, cal) at reader
def sc: date = schedule(month_of(d0), dom, following, cal) at reader

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun])
  cal6 = calendar(weekends [mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat])
  d0 = 2026-03-04 "plan"
  dom = 7 "plan"

ask a: nb law 2026-06-30
ask b: nb6 law 2026-06-30
ask c: ib law 2026-06-30
ask d: sc law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: refused: RUN-DOMAIN calendar cal has no business day
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
b: 2026-03-08
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
c: false
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
d: refused: RUN-DOMAIN calendar cal has no business day
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
